Oracle SQL Developer for VS Code — Connection Keepalive

Notes on stopping idle Oracle connections from being dropped by firewalls, load balancers, or VPNs when using the Oracle SQL Developer extension for VS Code.

TL;DR

Add these two properties under Connection → Advanced and reconnect.

Name	Value
oracle.net.keepAlive	true
oracle.net.TCP_KEEPIDLE	600

Where these go
Open the connection in the Oracle Explorer panel, right-click → Edit (or Update Connection).
Switch from the Details tab to the Advanced tab.
Click + Add and enter the name/value pairs above.
Save, then disconnect and reconnect. Connection properties are read when the JDBC connection is created; they do not apply to an already-open session.

These are standard Oracle JDBC thin-driver connection properties, so the same values work anywhere the thin driver is used (SQLcl, JDBC apps, connection pools).
